NegroniMetal change to metal2vulkan f6a96b7d, on top of m2v/0002 (applied by scripts/metal/fetch-sources.sh):
a compositor policy for the per-pixel emulations a UI compositor does not need.
- DevicePolicy::color_writes (ColorWritesPolicy: Exact = default, DeviceUnorm8, DeviceUnorm8Srgb), carried in
  ProfileFields (so in the fingerprint). Under DeviceUnorm8 each 8-bit unorm channel of a replace/opaque attachment
  takes the device's conversion (ChannelWrite::Device) in exact_writes, so color_writes() selects no rounding for it
  (no ~35 instructions per channel); DeviceUnorm8Srgb also leaves the 8-bit sRGB encode to the device (no ~70
  instructions + 4 KiB table read per channel). A driver row (DriverDeviation::MetalColorWrites) cannot do this: it is
  format-agnostic (every unorm/snorm/10:10:10:2 format) and no policy switches it off for an A/B.
- driver_facts DEVIATIONS: a DriverId::MESA_TURNIP row of Unorm8LinearFilter (Qualcomm vendorID 0x5143, every GPU,
  Mesa 25.0.7). "NegroniMetal: unmeasured on A730, accepted for a UI compositor [I]". Taken only under
  Unorm8LinearFilterPolicy::DeviceWithinOneCode (derive.rs accepted()); the filter path is already limited to
  R8/RG8/RGBA8/BGRA8 Unorm 2D samples.
The bridge chooses the policy from env NEGRONIMETAL_POLICY (flame/0007).

